WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.562
Think of attention as a learned weighting system for context.

00:00:03.562 --> 00:00:07.337
Suppose we are representing the pronoun it in a sentence.

00:00:07.337 --> 00:00:13.942
Several earlier words are available, but only some of them are useful for understanding what it refers to.

00:00:13.942 --> 00:00:21.037
The attention mechanism produces a score for the relationship between the current token and other available

00:00:21.037 --> 00:00:24.872
tokens. After normalization, those scores become weights.

00:00:24.872 --> 00:00:30.522
Tokens with larger weights contribute more of their information to the updated representation.

00:00:30.522 --> 00:00:36.142
Importantly, there is no hand-written rule saying “pronouns must attend to nouns.” The model learns useful

00:00:36.142 --> 00:00:42.342
patterns from training data. Also be careful with interpretation.

00:00:42.342 --> 00:00:47.207
An attention weight tells us how information is mixed in one head at one layer;

00:00:47.207 --> 00:00:51.697
it is not a complete explanation of why the model produced a final answer.

00:00:51.697 --> 00:00:57.006
Use attention to understand the computation, not as a perfect window into reasoning.
